### Run state

Whether a call needs the machine running, and whether it leaves it running or
stopped, is in each method's docstring as two lines, `Requires: ...` and
`Leaves the machine: ...`; this table collects them (a test keeps the two in
step). The calls that run to a point -- `run_for_emulated_seconds`,
`run_until_or_timeout` and the debugger's run-to methods -- leave the machine
STOPPED; call `bbc.debugger.run()` before anything that needs it running.
`launch()` starts the machine itself once it has connected, so a launch means
the same thing in emulated time on every host; `start_stopped=True` leaves it
stopped at the reset vector, having executed no instruction, for a test that
sets breakpoints or watchpoints before `bbc.debugger.run()`.

| Call | Requires | Leaves the machine |
|---|---|---|
| `Beebium.launch` | nothing | RUNNING |
| `Beebium.connect` | nothing | unchanged |
| `Beebium.expect` | a running machine, unless the text is already on the screen | unchanged |
| `Beebium.boot_disc` | any run state | RUNNING |
| `Beebium.wait_until_ready` | a running machine | unchanged |
| `Beebium.run_for_emulated_seconds` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `Beebium.run_until_or_timeout` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `Debugger.run` | a stopped machine | RUNNING |
| `Debugger.stop` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `Debugger.reset` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `Debugger.step` | a stopped machine | STOPPED |
| `Debugger.step_cycles` | a stopped machine | STOPPED |
| `Debugger.ensure_running` | any run state | RUNNING |
| `Debugger.ensure_stopped` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `Debugger.running` | any run state | as it was on entry |
| `Debugger.wait_for_stop` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `Debugger.run_and_wait_for_stop` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `Debugger.run_to_cycle` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `Debugger.run_to` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `Debugger.measure` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `Keyboard.type` | any run state | unchanged |
| `Keyboard.wait_until_typing_complete` | a running machine, unless nothing is queued | unchanged |
| `Keyboard.wait_until_ready` | a running machine | unchanged |
| `Keyboard.press_break` | a running machine | RUNNING |
| `Keyboard.ctrl_break` | a running machine | RUNNING |
| `Keyboard.shift_break` | a running machine | RUNNING |
| `Keyboard.tap_caps_lock` | a running machine | RUNNING |
| `Keyboard.tap_shift_lock` | a running machine | RUNNING |
| `Keyboard.text_input` | a running machine | unchanged |
| `Video.capture_frame` | any run state; with after_cycle, a running machine | unchanged |
| `TubeSystem.run` | any run state | RUNNING |
| `TubeSystem.stop` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `TubeSystem.run_until_or_timeout` | any run state | STOPPED |
| `TubeSystem.run_for` | any run state | STOPPED |

