### gRPC fork support

Importing `beebium.client` sets `GRPC_ENABLE_FORK_SUPPORT=false` unless it is
already set. The client forks only to start processes, and grpcio's fork
handlers, run in a child forked while a channel is busy, can kill that child
before it starts. That happens only where a child really is forked -- on macOS,
or on Linux with a `preexec_fn` or `os.fork()`, since Linux `subprocess`
otherwise uses `vfork()`, which runs no fork handlers -- but the setting is made
everywhere. The setting must be made before grpc is first imported, so a
program that imports grpc itself, or another gRPC-based library, before
`beebium.client` should set the variable in its environment.

